  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q7",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the median and range of:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$12.5\\%,\\ \\dfrac{12}{5},\\ \\dfrac{7}{5},\\ 1.25,\\ 1.4,\\ 140\\%$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p22-q7-a-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Median: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1.4",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; range: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2.275",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Convert to decimals and order.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Divide percentages by $100$ and each fraction's numerator by its denominator: $12.5\\%=0.125$, $\\frac{12}{5}=2.4$, $\\frac{7}{5}=1.4$ and $140\\%=1.4$.\nOrdered data: $0.125,\\ 1.25,\\ \\underline{1.4,\\ 1.4},\\ 1.4,\\ 2.4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{Median}&=\\frac{1.4+1.4}{2}\\\\\\mathrm{Median}&=1.4\\\\\\mathrm{Range}&=\\mathrm{Max}-\\mathrm{Min}\\\\\\mathrm{Range}&=2.4-0.125\\\\\\mathrm{Range}&=2.275\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{17}{4}\\quad 2\\dfrac{1}{4}\\quad 5\\dfrac{3}{4}\\quad 7\\dfrac{1}{4}\\quad \\dfrac{31}{4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p22-q7-b-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Median: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "5\\frac{3}{4}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; range: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "5.5",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Order equivalent decimals; subtract the minimum from the maximum.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Divide each numerator by $4$; for mixed numbers, add the whole-number part. The equivalent decimals are $4.25,\\ 2.25,\\ 5.75,\\ 7.25,\\ 7.75$.\nOrdered data: $2.25,\\ 4.25,\\ \\underline{5.75},\\ 7.25,\\ 7.75$.\nThe third value is the middle value.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{Median}&=5\\frac{3}{4}\\\\\\mathrm{Range}&=\\mathrm{Max}-\\mathrm{Min}\\\\\\mathrm{Range}&=7.75-2.25\\\\\\mathrm{Range}&=5.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
